========================================
CLOUD ASSIGNMENT - STATIC WEBSITE HOSTING
USING NGINX ON AZURE LINUX VM
=============================

## STEP 1 : GIVE PERMISSION TO PEM KEY

Command:
chmod 400 vm1_key.pem

Purpose:
Provides secure read-only permission to the private SSH key file.

## STEP 2 : CONNECT TO AZURE VIRTUAL MACHINE

Command:
ssh -i vm1_key.pem azureuser@YOUR_PUBLIC_IP

Example:
ssh -i vm1_key.pem azureuser@20.2.83.37

Purpose:
Connects remotely to the Azure Linux Virtual Machine using SSH.

## STEP 3 : UPDATE LINUX PACKAGES

Command:
sudo apt update

Purpose:
Updates package repository information from Ubuntu servers.

## STEP 4 : UPGRADE INSTALLED PACKAGES

Command:
sudo apt upgrade -y

Purpose:
Upgrades all installed Linux packages to latest versions.

## STEP 5 : INSTALL NGINX WEB SERVER

Command:
sudo apt install nginx -y

Purpose:
Installs Nginx web server on the Ubuntu VM.

## STEP 6 : START NGINX SERVICE

Command:
sudo systemctl start nginx

Purpose:
Starts the Nginx web server service.

## STEP 7 : ENABLE NGINX AUTO START

Command:
sudo systemctl enable nginx

Purpose:
Ensures Nginx automatically starts whenever VM reboots.

## STEP 8 : CHECK NGINX STATUS

Command:
sudo systemctl status nginx

Purpose:
Verifies whether Nginx service is running properly.

Expected Output:
active (running)

Press:
q

to exit the status screen.

## STEP 9 : MOVE TO WEBSITE DIRECTORY

Command:
cd /var/www/html

Purpose:
Moves into the default website hosting directory of Nginx.

## STEP 10 : REMOVE DEFAULT NGINX PAGE

Command:
sudo rm index.nginx-debian.html

Purpose:
Deletes the default Nginx welcome page.

## STEP 11 : CREATE WEBSITE FILE

Command:
sudo nano index.html

Purpose:
Creates and opens the main webpage file.

